notes: Story-first only works if the document can keep up. When I tried to edit a real deck with an agent, two walls appeared. The first was mechanical. On a fifty-page deck, I'd ask for two pages to change. I'd get a new file. Then another. Defensive agents preserve instead of replace. The folder filled with near-duplicates and final versions, and I couldn't tell which one was the deck. Git had already solved this for code. The unit of change should be the page.
